  "question": {
    "text": "A bandwidth of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>MHz</mi></math> is available for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>.</mo></math> transmission. If the maximum audio signal frequency used for modulating the carrier wave is not to exceed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kHz</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The number of stations that can be broadcasted within this band simultaneously without interfering with each other will be __________.",
